# Delvers — consistency ledger

**Spoiler horizon: S1E02. Status: ASR-provisional, 2026-10-24.** Source-cutoff conclusions are not listening resolutions. The [dossier](../episodes/S1E01.md) owns timestamps and evidence; the [review queue](../REVIEW_QUEUE.md) owns bounded checks.

## Open questions

| Key | Issue | Current evidence and limit |
| --- | --- | --- |
| DEL-PREP-001 | Premiere publication versus spoken year | Publisher January 11, 2021 and original S1E1 title reconciled; both ASRs render opening year 2020. Recording date/spoken year remain unverified |
| DEL-PREP-002 | Audio-copy alignment | Both SRTs end about twenty seconds beyond matching local MP3 duration. No constant offset established; listening timestamps must be mapped before use |
| DEL-PREP-003 | Identities and spellings | Cast/roles established textually; matching preview/cast evidence supports Krandal Splenderbelt, Koh Spiros, Evelyn Grinkeeper as working forms. City, deity, supplier, patrons, farmer and dead delver remain provisional |
| DEL-S1E01-001 | Sacred Flame narration and adjudication | P/Q disagree on **would / wouldn't see** while engulfed, ~01:46. GM permits first cast despite discussed sight requirement; second uses corrected saving throw. Do not infer normal sight or silently rewrite the ruling |
| DEL-S1E01-002 | Earlier casualties and badge 542 | Bell reports Edgar's loss; Koh finds a dragonborn skeleton. Cassius identifies badge owner as Bran Broscale/Brosgail and describes a different mission. Exact name/cause/date unknown; no supported Edgar identity |
| DEL-S1E01-003 | Trophy enumeration and small-item custody | Koh mentions octopus eye, piercer eye and darkmantle tentacle; return accepts proboscis/tentacle/eyeball. Exact extra parts unknown. Shovel bought by Koh and used by Krandal, final holder unspecified |

| DEL-S1E02-001–005 | Crypt wording, contested mechanics and custody | See [S1E02 dossier](../episodes/S1E02.md) for recap address, House/Crush/Studwell/Kord, friendly fire versus two independent unconsciousness events, globe Daylight/Relentless Endurance, Sultan's sash and inclusive 300-gold compensation. All remain ASR-provisional pending targeted audio checks |

## Resolved provisionally by each episode's cutoff

| Subject | Bounded conclusion |
| --- | --- |
| Job outcome | Fissure sealed, concrete dries, trophies accepted, **120 gold actually paid / forty each**. Not merely a promise or a plan |
| Surviving lower creature | Only Koh directly sees it. Cassius later identifies his description as a grick. Sealed away from this route, not killed or captured |
| Drift globe and badge | Koh recovers both; **542 is badge number**, returned to Cassius. Globe cleared as nonsentient and left with Koh; powers explained but unused |
| Healing correction | Evelyn heals Krandal five. His Cure Wounds to her becomes **seven** after retroactive +one correction; his self-heal caps at ten. No full health or spell-slot recovery inferred at cutoff |
| Fire/evil misconception | Evelyn attributes Krandal's radiance to the creature; no demonstrated monster lightning. Failed Divine Sense is a creature-type limitation, not absence of all threats |
| Separated knowledge | Ceiling warning initially private to Krandal, shared ~02:01. Lower pursuer seen only by Koh, described later. No retroactive shared vision |
| Guides and compensation | Evelyn discards the returned book. One gold left under cart seat, not confirmed received. Horse/owner not attacked despite later banter |
| Next day and advancement (S1E01 cutoff) | Crypt assigned and lodging accepted, without a played long rest in S1E01. The rest and level-two advancement are established at S1E02 opening, and that day's crypt mission is completed; no subsequent rest or new XP amount established |
| Campaign boundary | Opening Wastes tavern remark is production framing; covered Eye of Grumsh-like trophy is not evidence for the Wastes Eye of Groxl |

